    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0522" n="508" xml:id="pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.918/6–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-20">June 20,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:56 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1295. Entirely approve suggestion Department’s 729, 19th.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d369-f1"/> My query to Lomuto was “while recently there has not been
                    active censorship of <hi rendition="#italic">Time</hi> magazine, from previous
                    experiences they have learned that none of their copies printed in Argentina
                    will be permitted to go through the mail if they contain any critical comment on
                    situation here, accordingly they have blanked out articles on Argentina as in
                    case of last two issues (there have been many previous instances). This in
                    effect is censorship and therefore pursuant to your statement to me will <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Time</hi> henceforth, irrespective of how critical the
                    article may be, enjoy full liberty of press? Will it go through mails without
                    slightest hindrance or delay and may I so inform <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Time’s</hi> representative?” To this Lomuto replied in most positive terms
                    there would be no hindrance or delay in post office or otherwise irrespective of
                    articles it might contain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
